{
  "abstract": "For every fixed complex dimension d at least two, this formalization constructs the specified orthonormal bases of homogeneous holomorphic polynomials in every degree N at least zero. On the complex unit sphere in C^d with surface measure normalized to mass one, the family has Kronecker-delta Gram integrals and spans the full degree-N monomial space. A positive constant depending only on d bounds every basis function on the closed complex Euclidean unit ball, uniformly in N. The explicit formula uses finite Fourier minors, increasing stars-and-bars indices, a square-root-of-two quadratic phase, and the normalization sqrt((N+d-1)!/((d-1)! product alpha_i!)). The proof includes anisotropic cancellation for the actual coupled quadratic form, full zero-extended Poisson finite differences, multinomial conditioning, and Gaussian evaluation of sphere moments. Here explicit refers to the basis formula, not an optimized numerical value of C_d.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Mark Lewko"
    }
  ],
